      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "As above, likelihood functions are constructed by standard conditioning arguments, using Equation 13.25b. For example, consider a collection of $n$ full sibs from the $i$th family, with trait values $y_{i1},\\cdots,y_{in}$ (taking values of zero or one). The likelihood for the $j$th sib from this family, conditioned on it having parental genotypes $g_{f}$ and $g_{m}$, is",
