    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Using Equations 13.11a,b to average over all possible parental genotypes yields the unconditional likelihood for this family. The resulting likelihood has four unknown parameters: allele frequency p, and the gene effects as measured by the three penetrances $ \\psi_{i} $. Curtis and Stam (1995) note that this likelihood parameter space can be reduced when an estimate of the population prevalence K is available, as this imposes the restriction given by Equation 13.27 on the four parameters.",
